    "created_at": "2016-07-19T01:00:11Z",
    "updated_at": "2016-07-19T01:00:11Z",
    "body": "Using current for source is pretty bizarre, no? It would mean that same-origin postMessage would always see the source as the receiver of the message, rather than the sender.\n\nIf Blink really does set source = current that's strong evidence of web-compatibility, but it seems pretty surprising and we might as well avoid it if we can. I wouldn't keep the incumbent concept around just for this, but if we need it for referrer anyway, I think we should use incumbent here.\n",
